#. §25: `a ∈ A`
#. §26: `ha : a ∈ A`
#: Game/Doc/Definition.lean:294
msgid ""
"[Doc.Definition] Nonempty\n"
"§0\n"
"for §1, §2, §3 means T is non-empty\n"
"for §4, §5, §6 means §7; check this with §8\n"
"As goal:\n"
"given §9, §10, use §11\n"
"given §12, §13 such that §14, §15, use §16\n"
"As assumption:\n"
"given §17, use §18 to obtain §19, §20\n"
"given §21, use §22 to obtain §23, §24, §25, §26"
msgstr ""
"For a set (or rather: a “type”) §1, the statement §3 means that some element in §1 (“of type §1”) exists. \n"
"Similarly, for a subset §5, the expression §6 is equivalent to §7. You can easily verify this equivalence using §8.\n"
"\n"
"## §0 as goal\n"
"\n"
"If you're already given or have constructed some element §10, you can prove §3 using §11. \n"
"Similarly, if you have an element §12 such that §14, you can prove §6 using §16.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"## §0 as assumption\n"
"\n"
"For a set §1, you can extract some §20 from the assumption §17 using §18. \n"
"For a subset §5, you can extract a §23 with §26 from the assumption §21 using §22."

#. §0: `A : Set T`
