#. §2: `A`
#. §3: `h : Set.Finite A`
#. §4: `h.toFinset : Finset T`
#. §5: `A`
#: Game/Doc/Definition.lean:335
msgid ""
"For a subset §0, §1 means that §2 has only a finite number of elements.\n"
"If §3 is given as an assumption, then §4 is the same subset §5,\n"
"but now explicitly understood as a finite subset."
msgstr "For a subset §0, the expression §1 means that §2 has only a finite number of elements. If §3 is given as an assumption, then §4 is the same subset §5, but now explicitly understood as a finite subset."

#. §0: `(A : Prop)`
#. §1: `(True : Prop)`
#. §2: `(False : Prop)`
#: Game/Doc/Definition.lean:345
msgid ""
"§0 is any statement, without further specification as to whether it is true, false, or\n"
"unprovable.\n"
"\n"
"See also §1 and §2 for the unconditionally true and false\n"
"statements, respectively."
msgstr ""
"§0 is any statement, without further indication as to whether it is true, false or unprovable. \n"
"\n"
"See also §1 and §2 for statements that are unconditionally true or false."

#. §0: `A ∧ B`
#. §1: `A`
#. §2: `B`
#. §3: `A ∧ B`
#. §4: `constructor`
#. §5: `A`
#. §6: `B`
#. §7: `A ∧ B`
