#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:397
msgid ""
"The §0 tactic breaks down an assumption into its individual parts.\n"
"\n"
"| before       | tactic                 | after                                   |\n"
"|:------------------ |:--------------------- - |:------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| §1        | §2 | §3 and §4                      |\n"
"| §5        | §6 | §7 and §8              |\n"
"| §9   | §10      | §11                                    |\n"
"| §12 | §13  | §14 and §15                     |\n"
"| §16        | §17   | a target with §18, a target with §19 |\n"
"\n"
"Type the brackets in the first four examples as §20 or §21.\n"
"Here, §22 is the *anonymous constructor*.\n"
"You can think of it as similar to the tuple notation in\n"
"“an abelian group is a tuple §23 such that ...”."
msgstr ""
"The tactic §0 splits an assumption into its constituent parts. \n"
"\n"
"| before | tactic | after | \n"
"|:------------------ |:---------------------- |:------------------------------------------ | \n"
"| §1 | §2 | §3 and §4 | \n"
"| §5 | §6 | §7 and §8 | \n"
"| §9 | §10 | §11 |\n"
"| §12 | §13 | §14 and §15 | \n"
"| §16 | §17 | one goal with §18, one goal with §19 | \n"
"\n"
"You can write the angle brackets in the first four examples as §20 and §21, respectively. The expression §22 is the *anonymous constructor*.\n"
"You can think of it as similar to the tuple notation in “an Abelian group is a tuple §23 such that …”."

