#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:515
msgid ""
"The §0 tactic attempts to apply a large number of lemmas to simplify a given expression.\n"
"(Technically, these are all lemmas in §1 that are marked with §2.)\n"
"\n"
"## Variants\n"
"\n"
"* §3 additionally uses the assumption §4 or the lemma §5 for simplification\n"
"* §6 additionally uses the definition of §7\n"
"* §8 exclusively uses the assumptions/lemmas/definitions §9, §10, and §11\n"
"* §12 shows you which lemmas were used"
msgstr ""
"The tactic §0 attempts to apply a large number of lemmas in order to simplify a given expression. \n"
"\n"
"## Variants \n"
"\n"
"* §3 additionally uses the hypothesis §4 or the lemma §5 for simplification \n"
"* §6 additionally uses the definition of §7 \n"
"* §8 exclusively uses the prerequisites/lemmas/definitions §9, §10 and §11 \n"
"\n"
"*(In reality, §0 is much stronger that in this game:  §0 uses all lemmas marked with §2 in §1.  Some of these can solve certain levels in this game in a single line. For the purposes of this game, we have therefore severely restricted the set of lemmas available to §0.)*"

#. §0: `simp_rw`
