#: Game/Doc/Tactic.lean:616
msgid ""
"With §0, you can write out the definition §1 in the proof goal.\n"
"With §2, you do the same thing, but in the assumption §3.\n"
"\n"
"Although the proof goal or assumption before and after §4 are identical in definition,\n"
"many tactics (e.g., §5 or §6) operate on a syntactic level;\n"
"they do not “see through definitions.”\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and Relatives\n"
"\n"
"The tactics §7 and §8 do practically the same thing."
msgstr ""
"With §0, you can spell out the definition §1 in the goal.\n"
"With §2, you do the same in assumption §3. \n"
"\n"
"Goal and assumption before and after §4 are definitionally equivalent, but tactics such as §5 or §6 operate on a syntactic level – they do not “see through” definitions. It can easily happen that they work only after (or only before) an §4.\n"
"\n"
"## Friends and relations\n"
"\n"
"For all practical purposes, §7 is equivalent to §8."

#. §0: `∃x, P x`
