msgstr ""
"**Scribble**: Bravo! Now let's get out of here before another queue forms! \n"
"\n"
"Queen Logwynn has fallen asleep in the meantime, and you slip away quietly."

#: Game/Levels/Logo.lean:21
msgid "Logo"
msgstr "Logo"

#: Game/Levels/Logo.lean:47
msgid "Intro Logo"
msgstr ""
"Due to an unforeseen and non-canonical singularity in space-time, you have accidentally stumbled into a parallel universe. It appears there is no going back. You had better prepare yourself to stay and find your way around. \n"
"\n"
"There are lots of friendly little planets orbiting around. All habitable, and with up to seven sunsets a day included.\n"
"However, they are inhabited by formalosophers, strange creatures with unorthodox mathematical obsessions. To make things worth, word has already spread that you were a mathematician in your previous universe. You will find no peace here until you learn how to satisfy their insatiable thirst for knowledge.\n"
"\n"
"There are two minor complications: firstly, the formalosophers appear to have no deeper understanding of mathematics whatsoever, and secondly, they communicate about mathematics exclusively in Leanish, a dialect that is completely foreign to you. \n"
"\n"
"Fortunately, Scribble has changed universes with you. Scribble is your little smart-elf. He may not be the mathematical genius you would have wished for in this situation, but it seems he already knows some Leanish from somewhere. And knowing some Leanish is a game changer in this place."

#: Game/Levels/Implis/L01_Intro.lean:14
msgid "Intro Implis L01"
msgstr "**Head of Operations**: Here, for example:"

#. §0: `\\to`
#. §1: `«{B}»`
#. §2: `«{A}»`
#. §3: `tauto`
#. §4: `h`
#. §5: `intro h`
#: Game/Levels/Implis/L01_Intro.lean:39
msgid ""
"Prove the implication (§0):\n"
"assuming §1 is true, §2 implies 'A and B' is also true. You cannot use §3.\n"
"Begin by assumption that A is true.\n"
"Choose a name §4 for this assumption and introduce it via §5."
msgstr ""
"**Head of Operations**: The workers think this is correct and that we urgently need it. But no one can prove it to me. \n"
"\n"
"**You**: One moment. This *is* an implication (§0) again! We assume that §1 holds, and we need to show that under this assumption §2 implies “§2 and §1”. Well, of course! That's obviously true.\n"
"\n"
"The Head of Operations looks at you expectantly. \n"
"\n"
"**You** *(softly to Scribble)*: Should I write down §3 for him? \n"
"\n"
"**Scribble** *(equally softy)*: The way he looks, I'm afraid he won't understand that either. Better write out the proof.\n"
"\n"
"**You**: But how? I'd like to start by saying something like “So let's assume that §2 holds …” \n"
"\n"
"**Scribble**: Yes, good idea. Just choose a name for your assumption, for example §4 as in “hypothesis”, and start with §5."

#. §0: `«{A}»`
#. §1: `«{B}»`
#. §2: `«{A}» ∧ «{B}»`
#: Game/Levels/Implis/L01_Intro.lean:51
msgid "Having §0 and §1 in your assumptions you have to show §2"
msgstr ""
"**You**: Okay. So now I have both §0 and §1 among my assumptions and need to show §2. \n"
"\n"
"**Scribble**: Exactly. And you already know how to do that."

#: Game/Levels/Implis/L01_Intro.lean:67
msgid "Conclusion Implis L01"
msgstr ""
"**Head of Operations**: Perfect! Thank you very much! \n"
"\n"
"He goes to a control panel and presses a few buttons. \n"
"Somewhere, a conveyor belt creaks loudly and starts moving. \n"
"\n"
"**Head of Operations**: Do you have a few more minutes?"

#: Game/Levels/Implis/L02_Revert.lean:19
msgid "Intro Implis L02"
msgstr ""
"The Head of Operations takes a stack of paper out of a container. \n"
"\n"
"**Head of Operations**: Quite a lot has accumulated here. It would be really great if you could help me a little more. \n"
"\n"
"He hands you the top sheet."

