#: Game/Levels/Spinoza.lean:38
msgid "Intro Spinoza"
msgstr ""
"**Scribble**: I think that's Spinoza, one of the very few asteroids of the QED type. Quick. We have to hurry a bit, otherwise we'll miss it. \n"
"\n"
"Half an hour later, you've landed. Spinoza doesn't look very inviting. Its entire surface is covered with fine, red dust. A single, lonely formalosopher, who introduces himself as Benedictus, is waiting for you.\n"
"\n"
"**Benedictus**: Glad to see you! I've been waiting for you! \n"
"\n"
"**You**: Do you also have some urgent questions …? \n"
"\n"
"**Benedictus**: Oh no, I'm past that age. But I can imagine what it was like on Implis and Quantus. And believe me, it's not much better on the other planets. But perhaps I can prepare you a little. \n"
"\n"
"**You**: Can't we just stay here and rest a while? \n"
"\n"
"Benedictus shakes his head. \n"
"\n"
"**Benedictus**: No. Spinoza cannot accommodate three inhabitants. And you must continue your journey soon, otherwise the return journey will become impossibly long. We only pass by the planets every 400 years or so."

