#: Game.lean:41
msgid "[Game] Introduction"
msgstr ""
"# Game Over or QED? \n"
"\n"
"Are you curious what computer-assisted theorem proving feels like compared to pen-and-paper mathematics? Then you've come to the right place! In this game, you will learn how to work with the proof assistant Lean 4 and the proof library mathlib.\n"
"You will verify sum formulas by induction, show that a map is surjective if and only if it has a right inverse, prove that there are uncountably many sequences of natural numbers, and characterise the trace as a map among all functions defined on the space of square matrices.\n"
"\n"
"The interface is somewhat simplified, but if you activate *editor mode*, it feels almost like VSCode, the standard IDE for Lean.\n"
"On a smartphone or tablet, it is better to stay in the default *typewriter mode* and turn off all autocompletion/autocorrection features of your on-screen keyboard (a.k.a. “smart typing”, “text recognition”, “predictive text” etc.). \n"
"\n"
"Click on the first planet *Logo* to start your journey.\n"
"\n"
"## Progress\n"
"\n"
"Your game progress is stored locally in your browser as *site data*. You can also download your progress via the menu and save it to your disk. Note that many browsers delete *site data* and *cookies* together. \n"
"\n"
"## Rules \n"
"\n"
"If you want to take the game seriously, keep the default setting *Rules: regular*.\n"
"If you just want to poke around, select *Rules: relaxed*.  This will allow you to access every level immediately, even if you haven't solved the previous levels yet.\n"
"\n"
"## News \n"
"\n"
"`[2026-05-21]` The game’s set of `simp` lemmas is now restricted to a small subset of the `simp` lemmas from `mathlib`.  If some of the levels you thought you'd solved now suddenly appear as unsolved, it's probably because you were using a `simp`le short-cut.\n"
"\n"
"`[2026-03-20]` The game is now available in English.  If you are interested in contributing translations to other languages, [please get in touch](https://github.com/hhu-adam/Robo/tree/main?tab=readme-ov-file#translations)!\n"
"\n"
"For background information and credits, see *Game Info* in the menu."

#: Game.lean:42
msgid "[Game] Info"
msgstr ""
"## Project ADAM \n"
"\n"
"This educational game was developed as part of the project [ADAM: Anticipating the Digital Age of Mathematics](https://hhu-adam.github.io/) project at Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf, funded by the *Freiraum 2022* programme of the *Stiftung Innovation in der Hochschullehre*.\n"
"Ongoing maintenance and development are generously supported by *Renaissance Philanthropy* through the *AI for Math Fund*.\n"
"\n"
"## Game content\n"
"\n"
"**Spoiler alert** You can find an overview of the rough mathematical content of all planets on [Github](https://github.com/hhu-adam/Robo?tab=readme-ov-file#overview-over-existing-content).\n"
"\n"
"## Credits\n"
"\n"
"* **Project management:** Marcus Zibrowius, Immi Halupczok\n"
"* **Game engine:** Jon Eugster, Alexander Bentkamp, Patrick Massot – see [lean4game](https://github.com/leanprover-community/lean4game?tab=readme-ov-file#credits)\n"
"* **Levels:** Jon Eugster, Marcus Zibrowius, Sina Hazratpour\n"
"* **Concept & Story:** Marcus Zibrowius\n"
"* **Translations:**\n"
"  * **en:** Marcus Zibrowius / DeepL\n"
"  * **es:** [Enrique Díaz](https://github.com/qdiazblanco), [Pepa Montero](https://github.com/pepamontero) / Claude\n"
"  * **zh:** [Shuai Zhao](https://github.com/LazyThree) / ChatGPT, [John Lu](https://johnlyu2.github.io) \n"
"* **Illustrations:** [Dušan Pavlić](https://www.behance.net/dusanpavlic#)\n"
"\n"
"## Contact\n"
"\n"
"The game is constantly being revised.\n"
"We welcome your feedback, suggestions, and criticism,\n"
"for example, by email to\n"
"[Marcus Zibrowius](https://www.math.uni-duesseldorf.de/~zibrowius/).\n"
"You are equally welcome create issue's on GitHub, be it for typos, bugs or feature requests:\n"
"\n"
"* Please submit issues regarding game content to the repository [Robo](https://github.com/hhu-adam/Robo/issues).\n"
"* Please submit issues regarding the server and our software to the [lean4game repository](https://github.com/leanprover-community/lean4game/issues)."

